---
import Icon from '../site/Icon.astro';
import { whitepaperUrl } from '../../lib/links';

// Checked against the January 2026 paper, the July 21 development update,
// the August 5 Moon Fork report and the public implementation repository.
// A published mechanism and a public codebase are not a deployment claim.
const developmentUrl = 'https://www.augur.net/blog/augur-testing-past-building-future/';
const forkReportUrl = 'https://www.augur.net/blog/post-fork-announcements/';
const sources = [
  {
    title: 'The proposed mechanism',
    description: 'Reporting, escalating bonds, forks and the economic assumptions behind the design.',
    status: 'Whitepaper · January 2026',
    label: 'Read the whitepaper',
    href: whitepaperUrl,
  },
  {
    title: 'The implementation',
    description: 'ChainSafe is building Augur Lituus in public, with the Lituus Foundation reviewing the work against the paper.',
    status: 'In development · Lituus-CS',
    label: 'Explore the code',
    href: 'https://github.com/AugurProject/Lituus-CS',
  },
  {
    title: 'Testing, audits and documentation',
    description: 'The work required before applications can depend on Augur Lituus. No launch date has been announced.',
    status: 'Ahead of application use',
    label: 'Read the development update',
    href: developmentUrl,
  },
];
---

<section class="research-evidence rm-frame" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-title">
  <div class="research-introduction">
    <h2 class="augur-type-display rm-section-title" id="research-title">A design you<br />can inspect.</h2>
    <p class="web-lead">Augur Lituus is in development. Start with the paper, follow the implementation, and examine the assumptions.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="research-reading">
    <ul class="research-sources" aria-label="Research and development sources">
      {sources.map(source => (
        <li>
          <h3 class="augur-type-heading-2">{source.title}</h3>
          <p class="source-description rm-body-small">{source.description}</p>
          <div class="source-reading">
            <span class="source-status">{source.status}</span>
            <a class="rm-link" href={source.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{source.label}<Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <div class="research-questions">
      <details>
        <summary class="augur-type-ui">How does this relate to earlier Augur?<Icon name="plus" /></summary>
        <div class="research-answer rm-body-small">
          <p>Augur began as a prediction market protocol with its own oracle. Augur Lituus extends the resolution layer to other markets and applications.</p>
          <p>The Moon Fork completed Augur v2’s first live fork on Ethereum on August 3, 2026. That is evidence from the earlier protocol; Augur Lituus remains in development.</p>
          <a class="rm-link" href={forkReportUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the Moon Fork report<Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary class="augur-type-ui">What is REP?<Icon name="plus" /></summary>
        <div class="research-answer rm-body-small">
          <p>REP is the token used for query fees and the bonds that back reports and challenges. In the proposed design, participants put REP at risk when they support an answer. A fork requires holders to choose a universe by migrating their tokens.</p>
          <p>Augur Lituus is being built around REPv2_Yes_1, the REP that migrated to the winning universe in the Moon Fork.</p>
          <a class="rm-link" href={forkReportUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the current REP context<Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .research-evidence { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.4fr); gap: clamp(48px, 7vw, 112px); padding-block: 104px; }
  .research-introduction { align-self: start; }
  .research-introduction .web-lead { max-width: 37ch; margin-top: 28px; color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .research-reading { min-width: 0; }
  .research-sources { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .research-sources li { padding-block: 28px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-quiet); }
  .research-sources li:first-child { padding-top: 0; border-top: 0; }
  .research-sources h3 { margin: 0; text-wrap: balance; }
  .source-description { max-width: 62ch; margin-top: 12px; color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .source-reading { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px 24px; margin-top: 20px; }
  .source-status { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .research-evidence :global(.rm-link) { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
  .research-evidence :global(.rm-link .web-icon) { width: 15px; height: 15px; flex: none; }
  .research-questions { margin-top: 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-quiet); }
  .research-questions details { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-quiet); }
  summary { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 24px; min-height: 68px; padding-block: 18px; cursor: pointer; list-style: none; color: var(--foreground); }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  summary :global(.web-icon) { width: 16px; height: 16px; flex: none; }
  summary:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 5px; }
  details[open] summary :global(.web-icon) { transform: rotate(45deg); }
  summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--foreground); outline-offset: 5px; }
  .research-answer { max-width: 65ch; padding: 0 32px 28px 0; color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .research-answer p + p { margin-top: 12px; }
  .research-answer > a { margin-top: 20px; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .research-evidence { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 48px; padding-block: 72px; }
    .research-introduction .web-lead { max-width: 55ch; }
  }
</style>
